  "measured_at": "2026-08-03T00:26:51Z",
  "merc_source_commit": "695fa1e9de0c3a8194ee79cc486cead4bc8887e0",
  "proves": "Gateway upstream-client connection-reuse overhead under a synthetic streaming stand-in. Side-by-side DefaultMaxIdleConnsPerHost=2 vs MaxIdleConnsPerHost=128 (production fix) at c=1,2,4,8,16,32,64. Primary evidence is connection/dial counts; TTFT includes a 50ms synthetic dial RTT so remote-pod shape is visible on loopback.",
  "root_cause": {
    "file_line": "control/realtime.go:637 (newRealtimeHTTPClient; was Transport: http.DefaultTransport)",
    "default_that_was_wrong": {
      "symbol": "http.DefaultMaxIdleConnsPerHost",
      "value": 2,
      "also": "http.Transport.MaxIdleConns default 100 would re-cap if only MaxIdleConnsPerHost were raised to 128"
    },
    "mechanism": "newRealtimeHTTPClient used http.DefaultTransport, inheriting MaxIdleConnsPerHost=2. Each concurrent streaming completion holds one TCP connection for the full stream. When a stream ends, only 2 idle keep-alives are retained per upstream host; the rest are closed. The next admission therefore cold-dials. At c=1 a single connection is reused (dials/ok\u22481/N). At c=32\u201364 dials/ok climbs toward 1 (almost every request dials). On a remote GPU pod each cold dial is TCP+TLS tens-to-hundreds of ms, which is the +TTFT and under-utilization tax.",
    "evidence_from_this_sweep": "Under the default arm, dials_per_ok_request rises from 0.05 at c=1 to 0.82 at c=64 and tcp_connections_opened tracks request volume (186 conns for 320 requests at c=64). Under the fixed arm, dials_per_ok_request stays at concurrency/requests (=0.20 at every level once c>=4) and tcp_connections_opened equals concurrency (64 conns for 320 requests at c=64). Completed request rate at c=64 improves from 1926/s to 2215/s (+15%) under identical stand-in load.",
    "why_free_at_c1_expensive_at_c32": "c=1: one connection, MaxIdleConnsPerHost=2 retains it, every subsequent request reuses \u2014 zero dial tax after warm. c=32: thirty-two concurrent streams; only two survive as idle; ~30 of the next wave pay cold dial. The cost is proportional to in-flight concurrency, not to anything about a single request body.",
    "money_locks_untouched": "Buyer funding serialization (evaluateRealtimeBuyerFunding advisory xact lock + FOR UPDATE) is preserved unchanged. This fix is only the upstream http.Transport idle pool."
  },
